## Richest Customer Wealth

## Problem
Given a 2D array accounts, where each row represents a customer and each element represents the money that customer has in a particular bank, find the maximum wealth among all customers.

## Approach
-- Treat each row as one customer.
-- Use an outer loop i to traverse each customer.
-- For every customer, initialize currentWealth = 0.
-- Use an inner loop j to traverse all the banks of the current customer.
-- Add each bank's wealth to currentWealth.
-- After calculating the total wealth of the current customer, compare it with highestWealth.
-- If currentWealth is greater, update highestWealth.
-- Repeat this for all customers.
-- Return highestWealth.

## Complexity
Time Complexity: O(m × n)
If it's an n × n matrix → O(n²)

Space Complexity: O(1)

SOLUTION
class Solution {
    public int maximumWealth(int[][] accounts) {
        int highestWealth = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < accounts.length; i++) {
            int currentWealth = 0;

            for (int j = 0; j < accounts[i].length; j++) {
                currentWealth += accounts[i][j];
            }

            if (currentWealth > highestWealth) {
                highestWealth = currentWealth;
            }
        }

        return highestWealth;
    }
}
